 data-label="Why">Condos sit longer; houses sell sooner</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You do not want to manage a roof, a pool or the building's insurance</th><td data-label="The better choice">A condo</td><td data-label="Why">The HOA takes care of the building</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rest depends on the building: its fee, its rules and whether a lender will finance it. The <a href="#the-building" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">building section</a> below lists what decides one.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="prices-over-time"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices over time">How have Myrtle Beach condo prices done compared with houses?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From its 2006 high to early 2012, the typical metro condo lost about 43 percent of its value. The typical house lost about 30 percent.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-cd-fig"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Typical condo and house value, Myrtle Beach metro</span><ul class="c3-cd-legend"><li><span class="c3-cd-line" style="background:#2f6f8f"></span>Houses</li><li><span class="c3-cd-line" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Condos</li></ul><svg class="c3-cd-chart" viewBox="0 0 360 262" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of the typical home value in the Myrtle Beach metro, monthly from late 2001 to September 2026. Condos rose from about $112,000 to a high of about $197,000 in November 2006, fell to about $113,000 in January 2012, rose to about $261,000 in October 2023 and were about $231,000 in September 2026. Houses rose from about $146,000 to about $364,000, and fell less after 2007."><rect x="56" y="30" wi